       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. This dose is also twice the maximum, and there's little evidence that going above about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day improves glycemic control. The main thing it adds is risk, mainly lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. For a dose that far out of range, I'd want a second check on it before it's entered.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Pharmacy or specialist confirmation.** Once pharmacy or the specialist has verified the dose, it can be entered under their authorization, such as an override or a documented protocol.\n- **A dose within the labeled range.** I can enter metformin 850 mg orally three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) now. The dose can be adjusted if the specialist confirms a different plan.\n- **A different regimen.** If the specialist's recommendation was misread, for example 1700 mg/day total, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
